  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.1. Increased capacity of Member States to ratify international labour standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In this biennium, on 22 March 2023, the Government of Iraq, in consultation with employers&#x2019; and workers&#x2019; organizations, has ratified two ILO Conventions: Social Security Convention No. 102 (C102) accepting parts II to X; and MLC, 2006 - Maritime Labour Convention, 2006 (MLC, 2006) in accordance with Standard A4.5 (2) and (10), with the specifications of the following branches of social security: medical care; sickness benefit; employment injury benefit. These two Conventions are expected to enter into force on 22 March 2024. 
The Ministry of Labour and Social Affairs in consultation with employers&#x2019; and workers&#x2019; organization and collaboration with the ILO will start procedures for the ratification of Convention 190 on &#x201c;Eliminating Violence and Harassment in the World of Work&#x201d;.
 The ILO has been providing enormous technical support for the Government and social partners to reach on ratification of the two Conventions and it will continue to provide technical support on the application and reporting of the newly ratified Conventions.</narrative>
   </description>
