  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.3. Increased capacity of Member States to engage in a forward-looking international labour standards policy</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The government of Iraq and Kurdistan Regional Government (KRG) have endorsed and launched a developed Labour Inspection Policy, and OSH Policy to implement the recommendations on reforming the inspection accordingly, as well as ensuring that the appropriate institutional arrangements and procedures are in place in line of the ILS ratified by the Iraqi government.    

The Government of Iraq ratified ILO Social Security (Minimum Standards) Convention, 1952, which is the foundation of all ILO Social Security Conventions. It outlines the minimum standards of the nine branches of social security: medical care, family benefit, maternity benefit, sickness benefit, unemployment benefit, employment injury benefit, old-age benefit, invalidity benefit, and survivors&#x2019; benefit. The ratification emphasizes the commitment of the government to enshrining social security as an inherent right and to reforming national legislation and regulations to strengthen legal protection and safeguards for workers and improve the business environment.
 ILO has provided the technical assistance required, to that reform process and support the Government of Iraq in its reporting responsibilities towards the ILO supervisory bodies.</narrative>
   </description>
